{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'sed -n 1,120p /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_10-13-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run/submissions/99d636940e67411f8595ab9c444b1924/raw.json 2>/dev/null | head -60; ls /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_10-13-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run/submissions/'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"rationale\": \"Fresh run. Oriented on the hashicorp/raft snapshot (root package is the execution package): state machine entry points in raft.go (runFollower/runCandidate/runLeader/leaderLoop), replication.go, commitment.go, configuration.go, api.go, snapshot.go, fsm.go. K3 (commitment) and (election up-to-date checks) read consistent with the documented rules, so I did not spend an investigation there. The first sourced uncertainty I am recording is in the authority-transition path: the explicit leadership-transfer API hands a caller-supplied ServerID to the transfer routine, and nothing in that path tests the target's suffrage, while the rest of the library (pickServer, electSelf, requestVote) treats 'is a Voter' as the precondition for holding leadership. Non-voter membership is a legal, documented public state (AddNonvoter), so this is an internally-supplied premise, not a prohibited-external-use argument. This update records sources, one investigation, and three behaviors; the discriminating experiment (3 voters + a caught-up non-voter, transfer to non-voter vs transfer to voter) is deferred to the next turn because the turn budget ends here.\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"api-transfer-to-server\",\n      \"file\": \"api.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 1268,\n      \"end_line\": 1284,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"initiate-transfer-check\",\n      \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 2187,\n      \"end_line\": 2199,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"leaderloop-transfer-target\",\n      \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 762,\n      \"end_line\": 784,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"startstop-replication-all-servers\",\n      \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 584,\n      \"end_line\": 592,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"timeoutnow-handler\",\n      \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 2208,\n      \"end_line\": 2215,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requestvote-highterm-stepdown-nonvoter-reject\",\n      \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 1663,\n      \"end_line\": 1684,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"electself-voters-only\",\n      \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 2013,\n      \"end_line\": 2020,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pickserver-voters-only\",\n      \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 2163,\n      \"end_line\": 2176,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    },\n    {\n99d636940e67411f8595ab9c444b1924\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
